[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) merged 412 reports about wrong dates into one issue. Read by cause, they
are two different bugs with two different fixes. Fixing the parser alone leaves the second one open.

<Callout kind="warn">
The merge followed [decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject): same subject, same issue.
Subject says nothing about cause, and the intake tag is only a browser guess.
</Callout>

## What is in it

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

The export has 427 rows. 15 are repeats of the same report id, so the count is 412.

## The two problems

1. **Parser reads dates month first: 379 reports** at 11 day-first tenants, April to October.
   Ticket: [issue 1](https://github.com/ArtiomKuzmenok/megadev-training/issues/1).
   Five of them (R-41202, R-41209, R-41236, R-41344, R-41620) read as one-day moves. The kb counts
   them where they are filed; they may be a separate timezone problem, to check after the fix.
2. **booking-v3 form hint says MM/DD/YYYY: 33 reports** from `form` at copper.studio,
   alder.physio and pale.harbour. People type month first because the form tells them to.
   Ticket: [issue 2](https://github.com/ArtiomKuzmenok/megadev-training/issues/2).

## Lessons

- Count by cause, not by subject. 15 of the 33 hint reports were tagged `parser` at intake.
- A ticket marked known is a claim. Re-read it against the data before you rely on it.

